A||||5||saleenfiero||Need help now!  (Alt related)||||5||
Z||000000||saleenfiero||03-11-2001||02:51 PM||||Ever since yesterday, I have been having probs with my car.  Keeps dying on me even after I charge the battery.  Is this alternator related?  I just put in another stereo amp in my car, so I know the power drain is more, but everything seemed fine till yesterday.  What can I check for?  Can you ground two car stereo amps to the same place and would this cause my problem?||||reg||5
Z||000001||saleenfiero||03-11-2001||03:12 PM||||Also, my voltmeter warning light inside the car (right next to the oil pressure) is sort of half lit up and half not.  What givez? ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||03-11-2001||05:39 PM||||Hey Saleen!<BR>  Sounds like your alternator died...<BR>    Try a voltage current test...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||87GTZ34||03-12-2001||01:55 AM||||Wow 1st post Fierowrecker!   Welcome to the forum.||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||03-12-2001||08:38 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/in-n-out.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/in-n-out.jpg</A>  <BR>running the amp behind the passenger seat i killed alternators left and right... the voltage regulators would choke and die. Streetwires and Scoche (sp) both make alternators that'll support more than just the car. and yes one grounding point is fine as long as the entire connector is touching the metal. and be sure your power/ground wires are large enough. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||saleenfiero||03-12-2001||11:25 AM||||I'm not running an amp behind the passenger seat.  Although I've got two behind the driver's side now.  Turns out it is the alt that's screwed.  We'll see how long the one I'm getting now will last!<P>------------------<BR>'86 SE - My car is actually a MacLaren F1 with a Fiero body kit; or not.||||reg||1
